# The wheel keys are momentary (ADR-0062): a press turns the wheel one notch,
# and the release after it is one the Sender drops (SendInput injects nothing
# for it, and the dry-run printer leaves it out). The Arbiter still sends it,
# so every press has its release in this trace.
# Knob ticks tap them: a clockwise tick taps WheelUp and a counter-clockwise
# one WheelDown, each a tap of 20 ms with a 20 ms gap.
# A hold of WheelDown (north, 1000 to 1300) turns the wheel once, not for as
# long as the button is down. Two overlapping holds of it (north from 1500,
# south from 1520) turn it twice, and the release comes with the last one's,
# at 1700. Ctrl+WheelUp holds Ctrl around the notch, and the sequence of
# WheelLeft and WheelRight taps each in turn.
+WheelUp@104
-WheelUp@124
+WheelUp@204
-WheelUp@224
+WheelUp@244
-WheelUp@264
+WheelDown@354
-WheelDown@374
+WheelDown@404
-WheelDown@424
+WheelDown@1000
-WheelDown@1300
+WheelDown@1500
+WheelDown@1520
-WheelDown@1700
+LCtrl@2000 +WheelUp@2000
-WheelUp@2300 -LCtrl@2300
+WheelLeft@2500
-WheelLeft@2520
+WheelRight@2540
-WheelRight@2560
